# Link
https://saaschurn.streamlit.app/

# Project Overview
Customer churn is one of the biggest challenges for SaaS businesses.
This project builds an end-to-end machine learning system to predict customer churn, prioritize high-risk customers, and explain predictions using XAI (SHAP).
The solution focuses on business usability, not just model accuracy, by using Top-K risk targeting and explainable insights to support retention decisions.

# Business Problem
Retention teams have limited resources
Not all customers can be contacted
The goal is to identify and prioritize the highest-risk subscriptions

#Key Question:
Which customers are most likely to churn, and why?

# Dataset Description
A fully synthetic but realistic SaaS dataset was used, designed to mirror real production systems.

# Model Selection
Baseline : Logistic Regression (for interpretability and validation)
Final Model : XGBoost Classifier

# Model Evaluation
Due to class imbalance, accuracy was not the primary metric.

# Metrics Used
Recall – minimize missed churners
ROC-AUC – ranking quality
Precision@K & Lift@K – business prioritization

# Final Performance
Recall (churn): ~79%
ROC-AUC: ~0.79
Lift@10%: ~4.2×
This means the model identifies churners over 4× better than random selection in the top-risk group.

# Top-10% Risk Strategy (Business Logic)
Instead of using a fixed probability threshold, customers are ranked by churn risk, and only the Top-10% highest-risk subscriptions are targeted.

# Impact:
Total subscriptions: 5,000
Top-10% high-risk customers: 500
Average MRR: ₹500
Average churn probability (Top-10%): 0.70
Retention success rate: 25%
Estimated Impact
Revenue at risk: ₹1.75 lakh / month
Revenue saved: ₹43,750 / month
Annual savings: ₹5+ lakh

SHAP was used to: Explain individual churn predictions, Identify key churn drivers

# Key churn drivers identified:
Recent usage decline
Days since last usage
Support response delays
Early subscription stage

# Deployment
The model was deployed as an interactive Streamlit application
Live Demo: https://saaschurn.streamlit.app/

# Tech Stack
Python | Pandas | NumPy | Scikit-learn | XGBoost | SHAP | Streamlit | Git & Git LFS


# Key Takeaways
Churn prediction is about prioritization, not accuracy
Temporal feature engineering is critical
Explainability enables action, not just insight
Top-K targeting aligns ML with business reality

